{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"c3d6318fc27915db6b5c7fcf67b90bbae15048cdb317e6c0c0f114c160eec258","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM provider framework and architectural decision record","key_entities":["docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md","docs/llm-framework.md","docs/env-vars.md","providers.py","bedrock_model.py","capabilities.py","runner.py","config.py","provider_factory hook","ProviderSession","ModelProfile","provider_provenance","KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES","_GATEWAY_PROVIDER_NAMES","BedrockProvider","REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","REBAR_LLM_MODEL"],"problem_keywords":["ADR documentation","provider seam","support tiers","LLM framework","Bedrock","Anthropic","pydantic-ai","provider registry","verdict provenance","first_class tier","best_effort tier"],"propositions":["The provider seam is pydantic-ai's provider_factory hook; rebar owns a registry that intercepts infer_model before falling back to pydantic-ai's resolution, and unrecognized qualifiers raise a typed LLMConfigError.","Two support tiers exist: first_class (Anthropic and Bedrock with native builders, full capabilities, covered by tests) and best_effort (everything else through one OpenAI-compatible builder, tier determined by base_url presence or gateway membership).","Native Bedrock uses BedrockProvider with ambient AWS credential chain; inference-profile ids are required, on-demand ids fail; REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION must be set explicitly because boto3 does not resolve region from IMDS.","Verdicts are signed on every tier and stamped with provider_provenance (provider, model, endpoint_host, tier, capabilities) in an unsigned sidecar payload, giving consumers visibility but not cryptographic binding.","Five rejected alternatives are recorded with their evidence: in-process LiteLLM (model-layer duplication), gateway-fronted Bedrock (loses caching and observability), refusing off-tier verdicts (breaks local development), long-term API key in SSM (contradicts AWS guidance on Bedrock credentials), cross-provider fallback (masks the signal the cutover exists to surface).","Documentation in docs/llm-framework.md was contradicted or absent on provider resolution, Bedrock, tiers, temperature, retry/backoff, and numeric defaults; the ADR and docs are now aligned and executable commands have been verified."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785861804607843793,"uuid":"836ba668-1447-4f4e-836a-1f95b1fe9b71"}